\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 \ul \ulc0 \
\
A few tips about draw io:
\f0\b0\fs24 \ulnone \
\
This program is finicky and even I am still learning all the ins and outs of it. There are ways to animate connector lines but that involves some also finicky plugins, so I\'92ve tried to keep the connector lines representing conveyor belts, pipelines, etc. simple and to the point.\
\
****\
\
\
\
\
\
\
This is simply a library of visual icons created to represent the most common building elements of Satisfactory as of
\f1\b  Update 3
\f0\b0 . I\'92m not an employee of Coffee Stain Studios, nor am I any sort of programmer. Just a graphic designer who loves \'93Satisfactory\'94 and wanted a set of tools to create better layouts for my factory builds. \
\
HUB, Equipment Workshop, Constructors, etc., all have an icon here that can be dropped into and placed according to where you want that element in your factory layout. You can also use the pre-set Lines for Conveyor Belts, Power Lines, Pipelines and Railways.\
\

\f1\b\fs36 \
\
\
Be aware:
\fs24 \
\
1. 
\f0\b0 draw io has limitations that don\'92t let it *quite* match how things lay out in-game. When you go to set a conveyor or pipeline, its default will most likely lay it out in the neat 90-degree curves and not direct or \'912D/Constructor/Noodle\'92 options we\'92re used to having available. \
\
If you find a way to alter these in draw io, feel free to let me know or announce in the reddit sub for the game at r/SatisfactoryGame. Power Lines also will be straight from A to B, not a graceful little curve like the way they hang in-game.\
\

\f1\b \
\
2. This set of tools is not meant to exactly mimic how things lay out in-game, but instead to just give you a better set of tools for more accurately planning a factory build.
\f0\b0  \
\
The buildings and elements are in-scale relative to each other (So a foundation block of 8x8 will be to the same scale of, for example, the Storage Containers that are 10x5).\
\

\f1\b \
\
\
3. DO NOT RESIZE ELEMENTS SEPARATELY. 
\f0\b0 Everything here should be useful as-is, but if you feel you need to resize things, make sure to resize them ALL, so they retain their relative scales to each other.\
\
\
\
4. The application doesn\'92t \'93snap\'94 elements quite the same as the game does, but it\'92s very close so with some attention to placement, you should be able to approximate the layouts of your in-game builds quite closely.\
\
\
5. Some of these elements don\'92t perfectly mimic their silhouettes in-game. This is a bit of artistic license to adjust for draw io\'92s limitations and requirements so as to best allow the connectors to join up to the shapes in the best approximation of conveyors/pipelines.\
\
\
\
